{"name":"Kinder","hex":"#b8bfca","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Kinder","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname.","Places in the United States:\nAn unincorporated community in Johnson County, Indiana.\nA town in Allen Parish, Louisiana.\nAn unincorporated community in Stoddard County, Missouri.\nAn unincorporated community in Lincoln County, West Virginia."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Kinder"}],"entries":[{"title":"Kinder (brand)","blocks":[{"text":"Kinder is an Italian brand of chocolate produced by Italian multinational confectionery company Ferrero. Products under the Kinder brand include several varieties and are sold in over 170 countries worldwide."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/Kinder_%28Wortmarke%29_logo.svg/330px-Kinder_%28Wortmarke%29_logo.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kinder_(brand)","wikidata":"Q15410057"},{"title":"Kinder Surprise","blocks":[{"text":"Kinder Surprise, also known as Kinder Egg or Kinder Surprise Egg, is a milk chocolate consisting of a chocolate egg surrounding a yellow plastic capsule with a small toy inside. Manufactured by the Italian company Ferrero since 1974, it was co-created by Michele Ferrero and William Salice, and is one of several candies sold under the Kinder brand."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Kinder_Surprise_Logo_%28English%29.png/330px-Kinder_Surprise_Logo_%28English%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kinder_Surprise","wikidata":"Q181042"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Sweets_002.JPG/500px-Sweets_002.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Sweets_002.JPG/1280px-Sweets_002.JPG?u